<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>
	<!--
		Missing body part penalty - settings section. These rows feed the C# half
		(CarryCapacityMissingParts.dll in Common/Assemblies); they do NOT patch any defs.
		The DLL reads the values once at startup via XmlExtensions.SettingsManager and only
		acts when the section's master checkbox (ToggleSectionMissingParts, created by
		CCFB_Section, default OFF) is ticked. Defaults here MUST stay in sync with the
		compiled defaults in MissingPartsBootstrap.cs.
		Values are PERCENTAGES of the pawn's base capacity (body size x 35 kg), positive,
		stored as plain percent numbers (XE percent fields save the percent number, e.g. "25").
		Value design (June 2026, VitaKaninen's table): children of each limb sum EXACTLY to
		their parent (femur 15 + tibia 5 + foot 5 = leg 25; clavicle 5 + arm 10 = shoulder 15;
		humerus 2.5 + radius 2.5 + hand 5 = arm 10; 5 fingers/toes = hand/foot 5), so with
		default values the per-limb cap is a safety net, not a daily occurrence.
		Spine and Pelvis share ONE row/key (MissingPartSpinePelvis): each needs the other, so
		the worse of the two counts and it is not doubled if both are gone.
		Row args for CCFB_PartRow: key | label | toggle default | percent default | section tag | tooltip.
	-->
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_Section</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>Missing body parts</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>false</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>

	<!-- Explainer text at the top of the section body (inserted BEFORE the SplitColumn),
	     then the total-reduction cap as the first setting. Guarded on the cap key. -->
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.Conditional">
		<xpath>Defs/XmlExtensions.SettingsMenuDef[modId="Vita.CarryCapacityFromBionics"]/settings//li[key="MissingPartMaxReduction"]</xpath>
		<caseFalse>
			<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.PatchOperationInsert">
				<xpath>Defs/XmlExtensions.SettingsMenuDef[modId="Vita.CarryCapacityFromBionics"]/settings//li[tag="CCFB_MissingParts"]</xpath>
				<value>
					<li Class="XmlExtensions.Setting.Text">
						<text>Each enabled part below reduces a pawn's mass carry capacity (inventory and caravan weight) by a percentage of their base capacity while that part is missing. Base capacity is body size x 35 kg - 35 kg for an adult human, less for children - so the penalties scale with age and size. Damaged parts count in proportion to lost HP, and bionics, prosthetics and other replacements count as present. A safety net keeps the math sane: only the topmost missing part is counted, and a limb's combined reductions can never exceed the value of its topmost part - losing pieces of a limb never costs more than losing the whole limb. Hover any row for details.</text>
					</li>
					<li Class="XmlExtensions.Setting.Gap">
						<spacing>12</spacing>
					</li>
				</value>
			</Operation>
			<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.PatchOperationAdd">
				<xpath>Defs/XmlExtensions.SettingsMenuDef[modId="Vita.CarryCapacityFromBionics"]/settings//li[tag="CCFB_MissingParts"]/leftCol</xpath>
				<value>
					<li Class="XmlExtensions.Setting.Text">
						<text>Cap reduction to this amount</text>
						<tooltip>The combined reduction can never exceed this share of the pawn's base capacity. At 100%, a completely mangled pawn can lose all of it (0 kg left) - they still wear gear, wield weapons and eat normally. Lower it to guarantee every pawn keeps some carrying capacity.</tooltip>
					</li>
				</value>
			</Operation>
			<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.PatchOperationAdd">
				<xpath>Defs/XmlExtensions.SettingsMenuDef[modId="Vita.CarryCapacityFromBionics"]/settings//li[tag="CCFB_MissingParts"]/rightCol</xpath>
				<value>
					<li Class="XmlExtensions.Setting.Numeric">
						<decimals>1</decimals>
						<percent>true</percent>
						<key>MissingPartMaxReduction</key>
						<label>Maximum reduction</label>
						<defaultValue>100</defaultValue>
					</li>
				</value>
			</Operation>
			<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.PatchOperationAdd">
				<xpath>Defs/XmlExtensions.SettingsMenuDef[modId="Vita.CarryCapacityFromBionics"]/settings//li[@Class="XmlExtensions.Setting.Button"][key="ToggleSectionMissingParts"]/actions/li/keys</xpath>
				<value>
					<li>MissingPartMaxReduction</li>
				</value>
			</Operation>
		</caseFalse>
	</Operation>

	<!-- Per-part rows, in body-tree order (spine/pelvis, then leg subtree, then arm subtree) -->
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartSpinePelvis</li>
			<li>Spine/Pelvis</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>20</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>One penalty for the pair: each needs the other to work, so the worse of the two counts and it is not doubled if both are gone. A pawn missing either cannot walk, but the value still cuts their inventory space and their share of a caravan's weight pool.</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartLeg</li>
			<li>Leg (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>25</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>Top of the leg. Caps the whole leg: femur, tibia, foot and toes together can never subtract more than this value.</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartFemur</li>
			<li>Femur (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>15</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>Inner thigh bone - can be destroyed while the leg itself survives.</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartTibia</li>
			<li>Tibia (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>5</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>Inner shin bone - can be destroyed while the leg itself survives.</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartFoot</li>
			<li>Foot (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>5</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>If the whole leg is gone, only the leg value applies - the foot is not charged again.</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartToe</li>
			<li>Toe (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>1</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>Per missing toe (5 per foot).</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartShoulder</li>
			<li>Shoulder (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>15</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>Top of the arm. Caps the whole arm: clavicle, arm, bones, hand and fingers together can never subtract more than this value. Bionic and prosthetic arms install here - a replaced shoulder has no penalty.</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartClavicle</li>
			<li>Clavicle (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>5</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>Collarbone - can be destroyed while the shoulder itself survives.</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartArm</li>
			<li>Arm (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>10</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>Arm severed below the shoulder.</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartHumerus</li>
			<li>Humerus (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>2.5</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>Inner upper-arm bone - can be destroyed while the arm itself survives.</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartRadius</li>
			<li>Radius (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>2.5</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>Inner forearm bone - can be destroyed while the arm itself survives.</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartHand</li>
			<li>Hand (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>5</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>If the whole arm is gone, only the arm or shoulder value applies - the hand is not charged again.</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="XmlExtensions.ApplyPatch">
		<patchName>CCFB_PartRow</patchName>
		<arguments>
			<li>MissingPartFinger</li>
			<li>Finger (each)</li>
			<li>false</li>
			<li>1</li>
			<li>MissingParts</li>
			<li>Per missing finger (5 per hand).</li>
		</arguments>
	</Operation>
</Patch>
